              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+magmas"} associative magmas
            %em groupoids
            (now clashing with the modern use of
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Garrett+Birkhoff"}> Garrett Birkhoff
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Hausdorff Groupoids
              %strong 35
              2 (1934) 351-360 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1968437"}> jstor:1968437
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1968437"} doi:10.2307/1968437
          %p
            The modern terminology “monoid” for unital associative magmas is (according to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Hollings09"} Hollings 2009, p. 529
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Bourbaki"}> Nicolas Bourbaki
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%89l%C3%A9ments+de+Math%C3%A9matique"} Éléments de Mathématique
              (1943)
          %p For more on the history of the notion:
          %ul
            %li#Hollings09
              %p
                Christopher Hollings,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Early Development of the Algebraic Theory of Semigroups
                %strong 63
                (2009) 497–536 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00407-009-0044-3"}> doi:10.1007/s00407-009-0044-3
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Math.SE,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/q/338281/381"} Who invented Monoid?
          %p
            Exposition of basics of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+algebra"} categorical algebra
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes"} geometry of physics – categories and toposes
              , Section 2:
              %em
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#BasicNotionsOfCategoricalAlgebra"} Basic notions of categorical algebra
          %p
            Properties of monoids expressed through properties of their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
          %ul
            %li
              Jens Hemelaer, Morgan Rogers,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Monoid Properties as Invariants of Toposes of Monoid Actions
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.10513"} arXiv:2004.10513
          %p
            Formalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+objects"} monoid objects
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structures"} mathematical structures
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+assistants"} proof assistants
          %p
            in a context of plain
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mart%C3%ADn+Escard%C3%B3"}> Martín Escardó
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~mhe/HoTT-UF-in-Agda-Lecture-Notes/HoTT-UF-Agda.html#magmasandmonoids"} The Types of Magmas and Monoids
              %em Introduction to Univalent Foundations of Mathematics with Agda
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.00580"}> arXiv:1911.00580
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~mhe/HoTT-UF-in-Agda-Lecture-Notes/HoTT-UF-Agda.html"} webpage
          %p
